  "question": {
    "text": "A planoconvex lens has thickness of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math> When placed on a horizontal table, with the curved surface in contact with it, the apparent depth of the bottom most point of the lens is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the lens is inverted such that the plane face is in contact with the table, the apparent depth of the centre of the plane face is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The focal length of the lens is (assume thickness of lens to be negligible)",
    "image": null
  },
